- Be concise 

# Writing code
- don't write excessive comments 
- use meaningful for variables
- create utility function and extract common logic
- emit LLM friendly error messages
- ALWAYS write e2e fixture tests 
- do write unit tests, and ensure high test coverage
- don't create lots of small test files, prefer creating logical file with multiple test cases
- ALWAYS run `bun test` and `bun tsc` to test the changes

# Writing plans
- Include code snippets and file paths
- Include mermaid diagrams
- Do not over-engineer, keep the design simple
- Ask clarifying questions
- Always prefer reuse over new code
- Include testing 
- Write bullet points
- Include, problem and solution